    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The frai-core test suite is now fully fixed and passing! Here's what I did:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **governance.test.js failure** (`Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')`):\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `finetune/index.js`, but it was only available in the default export\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n2. **eval/index.test.js failure** (`expected +0 to be 1`):\n   - The `toxicityMetric` function was being called with `(outputs, references)` from `runEvaluations`, but expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` \n   - This caused the references array to be incorrectly treated as banned terms, flagging all outputs as toxic\n   - **Fix**: Updated the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to match the API of other metric functions\n\n## Results\n\n\u2705 All 28 tests now pass across 8 test files:\n- `governance.test.js`: 5/5 tests passing\n- `eval/index.test.js`: 3/3 tests passing  \n- All other test files remain green\n\nThe fixes preserve all existing public exports and don't modify any test files.",
